🏛️ 1. Start the Redis Engine
Run this to create the database that will store your dashboard and task caches:

Bash
docker run --name devcollab-redis -p 6379:6379 -d redis
Engine: Runs in the background on port 6379.

🏛️ 2. Start the Redis Insight UI
Run this to launch the graphical dashboard for visualizing your JSON data:

Bash
docker run -d --name redisinsight -p 5540:5540 redis/redisinsight:latest
UI: Accessible via your browser at http://localhost:5540.

🏛️ 3. Connect the "Magic Bridge"
Open the UI and use this specific connection string to jump from the UI container to the DB engine:

Connection URL: redis://default@host.docker.internal:6379

host.docker.internal: Tells the UI to look at your laptop's ports instead of its own.

default: The standard administrative user.

🏛️ 4. Quick Verification
Verify the link is active by creating a key in the CLI and viewing it in the browser:

CLI: docker exec -it devcollab-redis redis-cli.

Command: SET test_key "Bridge is active".

UI: Refresh the Browser tab in Redis Insight to see the key.
